    "A Super Puma H225 water bombing helicopter crashed into the Barito River while conducting firefighting operations.",
    "Two crew members, reported as foreign nationals, survived the incident, while one crew member was found deceased.",
    "The National Disaster Management Agency (BNPB) confirmed that current firefighting efforts remain unaffected by the accident."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A Super Puma H225 helicopter operated by the National Disaster Management Agency (BNPB) crashed into the Barito River in the Tabatan village area of South Kalimantan. The aircraft was engaged in water bombing activities to suppress local forest and land fires at the time of the incident. Initial reports indicated that two pilots, identified as foreign nationals, survived the crash, while a third crew member of Indonesian nationality was initially reported missing. Subsequent updates from officials confirmed that the missing individual was recovered deceased. The authorities are currently investigating the circumstances surrounding the accident. Despite the loss of the aerial asset, the agency has stated that the ongoing efforts to manage regional forest fires will continue without disruption. The crash has prompted a rapid response from local emergency teams to secure the site and manage the aftermath of the event.",
